From f7cf577b83bf233582adf8cc1f0ab14d788deb3f Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: Jayanth Othayoth <ojayanth@gmail.com>
Date: Tue, 25 Aug 2026 02:42:00 -0500
Subject: [PATCH] plugin:CPER:Raw Add plugin support

Add support for the
xyz.openbmc_project.Logging.Extension.CPER.Raw extension.

Introduce a schema-backed descriptor and runtime plugin implementation
for CPERRaw metadata. Raw CPER payloads are validated against a
configurable maximum payload size, persisted using the artifact
utility, and represented through ArtifactRef instances stored by
the descriptor.

The plugin augments log entries with the
xyz.openbmc_project.Logging.CPER.Raw D-Bus interface and exposes
persisted raw CPER payloads through the GetFileHandle method.

Add a corresponding plugin factory and register it with the
plugin registry, enabling request-to-descriptor translation and
runtime plugin creation through the existing plugin manager framework.

Also add unit tests covering descriptor creation, plugin registration,
factory creation, payload validation, artifact persistence, payload
size enforcement, and raw artifact retrieval.

Tested:

'''
Tested:
    '''
    Generated a test CPER event with a 16KB raw  payload.

    busctl introspect xyz.openbmc_project.Logging \
      /xyz/openbmc_project/logging/entry/362

    ...

    xyz.openbmc_project.Logging.CPER.Raw interface -         -
    .GetCPERRaw                                   method    -         h

    xyz.openbmc_project.Logging.Extension.CPER.Processed interface -         -
    .DiagnosticDataType                           property  s
    .NotificationType                             property  s
    .SectionType                                  property  s
    .Oem                                          property  a{ss}

    xyz.openbmc_project.Logging.Entry interface -         -
    .Id                                            property u 362
    .Message                                       property s
                                                  "xyz.openbmc_project.State.Cper.Error"

    ...

    busctl --json=pretty call xyz.openbmc_project.Logging \
      /xyz/openbmc_project/logging/entry/362 \
      org.freedesktop.DBus.Properties GetAll \
      s xyz.openbmc_project.Logging.Extension.CPER.Processed

    {
        "DiagnosticDataType": {
            "data": "xyz.openbmc_project.Logging.CPER.Types.ContentType.CPER"
        },
        "NotificationType": {
            "data": "8f87f311-c998-4d9e-a0c4-fb4dfc2c8c14"
        },
        "SectionType": {
            "data": "dc3ea0b0-a144-4797-b95b-53fa242b6e1d"
        },
        "Oem": {
            "data": {
                "Source":
                    "/xyz/openbmc_project/inventory/system"
            }
        }
    }

    Verified that both CPERRaw and CPERProcessed metadata plugins were
    attached to the same log entry, demonstrating support for multiple
    runtime metadata plugins.

    Verified raw CPER data was persisted as an artifact:

    ls -l /var/lib/phosphor-logging/artifacts/

    -rw------- 1 root root 16384 Aug 25 07:47 cperraw-phzOwZ

    Verified persisted artifact size matches the generated 16KB CPER raw
    payload and is accessible through the CPERRaw interface.
    '''
'''

